-- allium: 3
-- issues.allium — issue tracking: issues, the conversation timeline, labels, milestones, and everything attached to an issue
--
-- Scope: the per-repository issue tracker and the conversation half of every
--   pull request. An `Issue` with `is_pull = true` is the conversation of a
--   `pulls/PullRequest`; every rule here applies to it unless it says otherwise.
-- Includes:
--   - Issue lifecycle: open (create), edit title / body / branch ref, close /
--     reopen, delete (repo admin), per-repository index shared by issues and
--     pull requests, due dates, lock / unlock with a reason, pin / unpin /
--     reorder with a per-repository limit (separately for issues and PRs).
--   - The Comment timeline: every comment kind (see `CommentKind`), including
--     the kinds created by `pulls` and `projects` rules (listed so the
--     timeline is one closed vocabulary); edit / delete of comments; content
--     history of issue bodies and comments (edits retained, at most
--     `content_history_limit` revisions; revisions can be hidden).
--   - Reactions on issues and comments, from an instance-configured set.
--   - Labels: repository labels, organization labels, exclusive scoped labels
--     (`scope/name`), archived labels, label templates and initialisation.
--   - Milestones: open / closed, due date, progress.
--   - Assignees and who may be assigned.
--   - Issue dependencies (blocked-by / blocking), optional cross-repository,
--     and the refusal to close an issue with open blockers.
--   - Time tracking: stopwatches, manual time, deleting time, who may track.
--   - Per-issue subscriptions (watch / unwatch; participants are subscribed
--     implicitly).
--   - Attachments: upload, allowed types, size / count limits, linking to an
--     issue or comment (release attachments are linked by `releases`).
--   - Issue templates (Markdown and YAML forms) and the template config
--     (`blank_issues_enabled`, contact links).
--   - Cross references (`#123`, `owner/repo#123`, `!123`) from issues,
--     comments and pull requests; keyword references in pushed commit
--     messages that close / reopen issues and log time.
--   - Mentions (`@user`, `@org/team`) resolved for notification.
--   - Blocked users (`accounts/UserBlock`) cannot open, comment, react or
--     change status; anonymous and read-only visitors.
--   - Per-repository issue / PR list filtering (state, labels, milestone,
--     project, assignee, poster, keyword) as surface exposure.
-- Excludes:
--   - Cross-repository / instance-wide issue search and indexers — `discovery`.
--   - Review, code comments, review requests, merge — `pulls` (their comment
--     kinds are enumerated here only).
--   - Project boards and card moves — `projects` (the `project` /
--     `project_column` comment kinds are enumerated here only).
--   - In-app notifications, mails, activity feed, RSS/Atom issue feeds,
--     reply-by-email — `notifications` (they react to the triggers below).
--   - Webhook deliveries — `webhooks`; workflow triggers — `actions`.
--   - Shadow copies of reported content before edit / delete — `moderation`
--     (it reacts to the edit / delete triggers, which carry the old content).
--   - Migrated "original author" fields, overriding `updated_at` on API
--     writes, and comment-type repair doctors — data-import concerns, owned by
--     the `migrations` addon.
--   - Timeline aggregation of consecutive label / review-request / status
--     events into one entry — presentation only.
--   - Rendering (Markdown, task-list checkbox counting, custom emoji images,
--     summary cards) — presentation; task counts are exposed as black boxes.
--   - Issue transfer between repositories and confidential issues — Forgejo
--     has neither.
--   - The legacy single `assignee` API field and the deprecated
--     `/issues/{index}/comments/{id}` API paths — Gitea API compatibility.
--
-- Emits:
--   IssueOpened(issue, mentions)                       -- issues only: a PR conversation is announced by
--                                                      -- pulls/PullRequestOpened, never by IssueOpened
--   IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)                  -- issues only: PRs close / reopen / merge through
--   IssueReopened(issue, doer, comment)                -- pulls (PullRequestClosed / PullRequestReopened / PullRequestMerged)
--   IssueDeleted(issue, doer)                          -- doer is null when an account purge removed it
--   IssueTitleChanged(issue, doer, old_title)
--   IssueContentChanged(issue, doer, old_content)
--   IssueRefChanged(issue, doer, old_ref)
--   IssueLabelsChanged(issue, doer, added, removed)
--   IssueLabelsCleared(issue, doer)
--   IssueMilestoneChanged(issue, doer, old_milestone)
--   IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment)
--   IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions)
--   IssueCommentEdited(comment, doer, old_content)
--   IssueCommentDeleted(comment, issue, doer)
--   ReactionAdded(reaction)
--   ReactionRemoved(reaction)
--   IssueReferencedByCommit(issue, commit_sha, pusher)
--   IssueCreatedWithProject(issue, poster, project)    -- projects puts the new issue on the board
--   UserViewsIssue(viewer, issue)                      -- external stimulus; notifications marks the thread read
--   OrphanedUploadCleanupFinished()     -- administration: the delete_orphaned_attachments run is done
-- Reacts to:
--   administration/OrphanedUploadCleanupDue(older_than) -- unlinked uploads older than that go
--   code/PushReceived(push)                            -- keyword references in commit messages
--   pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)      -- merger's stopwatch on the conversation stops
--   pulls/IssueClosedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer)    -- apply closing references
--   pulls/IssueReopenedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer)  -- apply reopening references
--   repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)   -- the tracker goes with the repository
--   access/UserLostRepositoryAccess(user, repository)  -- issue subscriptions and assignments there are dropped
--   repositories/CollaboratorRemoved(repository, user, doer)    -- unassign where the user may no longer be assigned
--   repositories/LabelTemplateApplied(repository, template_name) -- create the template's labels
--   repositories/RepositoryGeneratedFromTemplate(template, repository, doer, git_content, topics,
--       git_hooks, webhooks, avatar, labels, protected_branches) -- copy the template's labels
--   accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions)  -- drop or remove the user's traces
--   projects/IssueProjectChanged(issue, actor, old_project, new_project)  -- timeline `project` entry
--   notifications/MailReplyReceived(author, issue, replied_to, replied_to_code, body, attachment_count)
--                                                      -- a reply by mail becomes a comment
--   notifications/MailUnsubscribeReceived(user, issue) -- an explicit unsubscribe
--   moderation/ModeratorDeletesIssue(admin, issue)     -- delete an issue acting on an abuse report
--   moderation/ModeratorDeletesComment(admin, comment) -- delete a comment acting on an abuse report

use "./accounts.allium" as accounts
use "./organizations.allium" as organizations
use "./repositories.allium" as repositories
use "./access.allium" as access
use "./code.allium" as code
use "./pulls.allium" as pulls
use "./projects.allium" as projects
use "./releases.allium" as releases
use "./notifications.allium" as notifications
use "./moderation.allium" as moderation
use "./administration.allium" as administration
use "./keys.allium" as keys

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Black-box predicates and functions used below
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Permission predicates are thin local names for `access` semantics so that
-- rules read in tracker terms. "The issue's unit" is `pull_requests` when
-- `issue.is_pull`, else `issues`.
--
--   can_read_issue(user, issue)        = access/can_read(user, issue.repository, the issue's unit)
--   can_triage(user, issue)            = access/can_write(user, issue.repository, the issue's unit)
--   can_read_tracker(user, repository) = can read the issues unit or the pull_requests unit
--   can_manage_tracker(user, repository) = can write the issues unit or the pull_requests unit
--   is_repo_admin(user, repository)    = access/is_repo_admin(user, repository)
--   is_org_owner(organization, user)   = user is in organization.owners_team
--   can_be_assigned(user, repository)  = user is not an organization and has write
--                                        on any unit, or read on pull_requests
--   is_blocked(blocker, user)          = an accounts/UserBlock from blocker to user exists
--   is_blocked_by_owner(repository, user) = the repository's owner (user or org) blocks user
--   read-only gate: `requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})`
--       decided (administration 3): every user-initiated write below is refused
--       while the instance is read-only; reads (and UserViewsIssue's read marker,
--       part of reading) keep working. Reactions to other modules' events are not
--       gated here: the write that set them off was.
--   can_write_org_projects(user, organization) = organizations/can_write_unit(user, organization, projects)
--       (the board-write check projects applies to organization boards)
--   attachment_quota_allows(repository, size) = quota/quota_allows(<repository owner>,
--       size_assets_attachments_issues, size) (QuotaGate gate_issue_attachment; decided
--       quota 2: usage + size <= limit). Deleting or renaming an attachment never asks
--       the gate (decided quota 7).
--
--   kind_watchers(repository, is_pull) = users whose repositories/Watch on the
--       repository covers pull requests (is_pull) or issues (otherwise)
--
-- Exported for the migrations addon (decided: migrations 11):
--   assignable_named(repository, names) -> Set<accounts/User>
--       the local accounts with those names that satisfy can_be_assigned(_, repository)
--   resolves_to_assignee(repository, name) = some local account of that name
--       satisfies can_be_assigned(_, repository)
--
-- Repository issue-unit settings (REQUEST below):
--   timetracker_enabled(repository), only_contributors_track_time(repository),
--   dependencies_enabled(repository), closes_via_commit_in_any_branch(repository)
--
-- Text analysis:
--   resolve_mentions(issue, doer, text) -> Set<accounts/User>
--       `@name` and `@org/team` mentions; teams expand to active, non-blocked
--       members when the team has access to the issue's unit (or admin);
--       organizations are ignored; users who cannot read the issue, inactive
--       or login-prohibited users, users who blocked the doer and the doer
--       are dropped.
--   cross_references(repository, doer, title, text) -> Set<CrossReference>
--       `#N`, `!N`, `owner/repo#N` references (plus a preceding close /
--       reopen keyword), resolved against `repository` (where `#N` points),
--       that point at an existing issue the doer can read, found in the
--       title (null for a comment) and the text; see
--       `CrossReference`. A reference back to the posting issue itself is
--       dropped by the rule, not by the function.
--   commit_references(push) -> Set<CommitReference>
--   exclusive_scope(label) -> String     -- "" when not exclusive or no scope
--   is_allowed_file(name, head_bytes) -> Boolean   -- against config.attachment_allowed_types
--   template_is_valid(template) -> Boolean
--   task_count(text), tasks_done(text) -> Integer   -- `- [ ]` / `- [x]` items
--   is_lock_reason(reason)      = reason in config.lock_reasons
--   is_allowed_reaction(emoji)  = emoji in config.allowed_reactions

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Value Types
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A reference found in the text of an issue, PR or comment and verified
-- against the referenced issue and the doer's permission.
-- from: models/issues/issue_xref.go:161
value CrossReference {
    target: Issue
    action: XRefAction    -- `closes` / `reopens` only when the source is a PR, the
                          -- target is an issue, and the doer could close the
                          -- target manually (or is its poster / it is a new PR
                          -- in the same repository); otherwise `none`
}

-- A keyword reference in a pushed commit message.
-- from: services/issue/commit.go:106
value CommitReference {
    target: Issue
    action: XRefAction          -- closes | reopens | none
    commit_sha: String
    commit_message: String
    committed_at: Timestamp
    time_log: Duration?         -- `Fixes #1 @1h30m` logs time when closing
    branch: String
}

-- from: modules/structs/issue.go:234
value ContactLink {
    name: String
    url: String
    about: String
}

-- One field of a YAML issue form.
-- from: modules/issue/template/template.go:44
value IssueFormField {
    id: String?                 -- unique, alphanumeric / - / _ ; required except for markdown
    type: IssueFormFieldType
    label: String?
    required: Boolean           -- a hidden field cannot be required
    visible_in_form: Boolean
    visible_in_content: Boolean
    options: List<String>       -- dropdown / checkboxes
}

-- One label in a label template file.
-- from: modules/label/label.go:16
value LabelSpec {
    name: String
    color: String
    description: String?
    is_exclusive: Boolean
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Every kind of timeline entry. Kinds marked (pulls) / (projects) are created
-- by those modules' rules; everything else by rules in this file.
-- from: models/issues/comment.go:67
enum CommentKind {
    comment                       -- plain comment (Markdown, attachments)
    | reopen | close
    | issue_ref                   -- referenced from an issue
    | commit_ref                  -- referenced from a commit message
    | comment_ref                 -- referenced from a comment
    | pull_ref                    -- referenced from a pull request
    | label                       -- label added / removed
    | milestone                   -- milestone changed
    | assignees                   -- assignee added / removed
    | change_title
    | delete_branch               -- (pulls) head branch deleted
    | start_tracking | stop_tracking | cancel_tracking
    | add_time_manual | delete_time_manual
    | added_deadline | modified_deadline | removed_deadline
    | add_dependency | remove_dependency
    | code                        -- (pulls) code comment
    | review                      -- (pulls) review summary
    | lock | unlock
    | change_target_branch        -- (pulls)
    | review_request              -- (pulls) reviewer requested
    | review_request_removed      -- (pulls) review request withdrawn
    | merge_pull                  -- (pulls) conversation closed by merge
    | pull_push                   -- (pulls) commits pushed to head
    | project                     -- issue put on, moved to another, or taken off a board
    | project_column              -- reserved: Forgejo defines it but never records it
    | dismiss_review              -- (pulls)
    | change_issue_ref            -- issue branch/tag reference changed
    | pr_scheduled_to_auto_merge | pr_unscheduled_to_auto_merge   -- (pulls) auto-merge
    | pin | unpin
}

-- from: modules/references/references.go:62
enum XRefAction { none | closes | reopens | neutered }

-- Badge shown next to a poster in the timeline.
-- from: models/issues/comment.go:226
enum RoleInRepo { owner | member | collaborator | first_time_contributor | contributor | no_role }

-- from: modules/structs/issue.go:147
enum IssueFormFieldType { markdown | textarea | input | dropdown | checkboxes }

enum TemplateFormat { markdown | yaml }


------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An issue, or the conversation of a pull request.
-- from: models/issues/issue.go:90
entity Issue {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    index: Integer                       -- per repository, shared by issues and PRs, never reused
    poster: accounts/User
    title: String                        -- trimmed, at most config.max_title_length
    content: String                      -- Markdown body
    content_version: Integer             -- optimistic concurrency for body edits
    is_pull: Boolean
    status: open | closed
    closed_at: Timestamp when status = closed
    is_locked: Boolean
    ref: String?                         -- branch or tag the issue is about (issues only)
    deadline: Timestamp?                 -- due date, end of the chosen day
    milestone: Milestone?
    labels: Set<Label>                   -- decided: no priority field; priority is expressed with
                                         -- (exclusive, scoped) labels such as `priority/high`
    assignees: Set<accounts/User>
    mentioned_users: Set<accounts/User>
    read_by: Set<accounts/User>          -- users who have opened the issue page
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    -- Relationships
    comments: Comment with issue = this
    reactions: Reaction with issue = this
    attachments: Attachment with issue = this
    blocked_by: IssueDependency with issue = this
    blocking: IssueDependency with blocker = this
    tracked_times: TrackedTime with issue = this
    stopwatches: Stopwatch with issue = this
    watches: IssueWatch with issue = this
    pin: IssuePin with issue = this
    history: ContentHistory with issue = this
    pull_request: pulls/PullRequest with issue = this     -- the PR whose conversation this is (is_pull only)
    project_card: projects/ProjectCard with issue = this  -- the board card, at most one (projects/OneBoardPerIssue)

    -- Projections
    conversation: comments where kind = comment or kind = review
    issue_reactions: reactions where comment = null
    open_blockers: blocked_by where blocker.status = open
    active_times: tracked_times where is_deleted = false
    explicit_watchers: watches where is_watching = true
    explicit_unwatchers: watches where is_watching = false

    -- Derived
    num_comments: conversation.count
    is_pinned: pin.count > 0
    has_open_blockers: open_blockers.count > 0
    is_overdue: deadline != null and status = open and deadline <= now
    participants: comments.poster + { poster }
    -- Who follows the thread: an explicit watch, a watch on the repository's
    -- issues (or pull requests, for a PR), or having taken part; minus anyone
    -- who explicitly unsubscribed. Read by notifications and discovery.
    explicitly_unsubscribed: explicit_unwatchers.user
    subscribers: explicit_watchers.user + participants + kind_watchers(repository, is_pull) - explicitly_unsubscribed
    num_tasks: task_count(content)
    num_tasks_done: tasks_done(content)

    transitions status {
        open -> closed
        closed -> open
        terminal: closed
    }
}

-- One entry of an issue's timeline. The payload fields that apply depend on
-- `kind`; all others are absent.
-- from: models/issues/comment.go:244
entity Comment {
    issue: Issue
    -- decided: requests 1 — a comment a deploy-key push left (a pull request's
    -- push entry) records the key and no user; every other comment has a poster
    poster: accounts/User?
    deploy_key: keys/DeployKey?
    kind: CommentKind
    content: String                      -- Markdown for comment/code/review/dismiss_review;
                                         -- the lock reason for lock; the duration for time kinds;
                                         -- the date(s) for deadline kinds; the reviewer's or
                                         -- team's name for review_request (removals too);
                                         -- for pr_unscheduled_to_auto_merge, the failure reason
                                         -- when pulls removed a failing auto-merge (pulls decision 3)
    content_version: Integer
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    -- kind = label (label is cleared when the label is deleted; its name is kept)
    label: Label?
    label_added: Boolean?
    deleted_label_name: String?
    -- kind = milestone (cleared when the milestone is deleted; its name is kept)
    old_milestone: Milestone?
    new_milestone: Milestone?
    deleted_old_milestone_name: String?
    deleted_new_milestone_name: String?
    -- kind = assignees / review_request
    assignee: accounts/User?
    assignee_team: organizations/Team?
    assignee_removed: Boolean?
    -- kind = change_title
    old_title: String?
    new_title: String?
    -- kind = change_issue_ref / change_target_branch
    old_ref: String?
    new_ref: String?
    -- kind = add_dependency / remove_dependency
    dependent_issue: Issue?
    -- kind = add_time_manual / stop_tracking
    tracked_time: TrackedTime?
    -- kind = commit_ref
    commit_sha: String?
    -- kind = issue_ref / comment_ref / pull_ref: the origin of the reference
    ref_issue: Issue?
    ref_comment: Comment?
    ref_action: XRefAction?
    -- kind = project: the board after and before (either may be null: added,
    -- moved, removed); a board deleted since is shown as a "deleted project"
    -- placeholder
    project: projects/Project?
    old_project: projects/Project?
    -- kind = code / review / dismiss_review
    review: pulls/Review?

    -- Relationships
    reactions: Reaction with comment = this
    attachments: Attachment with comment = this
    history: ContentHistory with comment = this

    -- Derived
    has_content: kind = comment or kind = code or kind = review or kind = dismiss_review
    -- the kinds that carry user text or attachments (reportable; moderation)
    has_user_content: has_content
    accepts_attachments: kind = comment or kind = code or kind = review
    counts_as_conversation: kind = comment or kind = review
    is_edited: history.count > 1
    -- decided: timeline events of a deleted label or milestone stay, marked deleted
    label_is_deleted: deleted_label_name != null
    old_milestone_is_deleted: deleted_old_milestone_name != null
    new_milestone_is_deleted: deleted_new_milestone_name != null
}

-- A repository label or an organization label (usable in all the
-- organization's repositories). Exactly one of repository / organization.
-- from: models/issues/label.go:87
entity Label {
    repository: repositories/Repository?
    organization: organizations/Organization?
    name: String                         -- at most config.max_label_name_length
    description: String                  -- at most config.max_label_description_length
    color: String                        -- normalised to #rrggbb
    is_exclusive: Boolean                -- `scope/name` labels in one scope are mutually exclusive on an issue
    archived_at: Timestamp?
    created_at: Timestamp

    -- Derived
    is_archived: archived_at != null
    scope: exclusive_scope(this)
}

-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:48
entity Milestone {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    name: String                         -- trimmed, at most config.max_milestone_name_length
    description: String
    status: open | closed
    closed_at: Timestamp when status = closed
    deadline: Timestamp?                 -- absent means "no due date"
    created_at: Timestamp
    updated_at: Timestamp

    issues: Issue with milestone = this
    closed_issues: issues where status = closed
    open_issues: issues where status = open

    num_issues: issues.count
    num_closed_issues: closed_issues.count
    num_open_issues: open_issues.count
    completeness: percent(num_closed_issues, num_issues)    -- 0 when empty
    is_overdue: deadline != null and status = open and deadline <= now

    transitions status {
        open -> closed
        closed -> open
        terminal: closed
    }
}

-- A user's reaction on an issue (comment absent) or on a comment.
-- from: models/issues/reaction.go:62
entity Reaction {
    user: accounts/User
    issue: Issue
    comment: Comment?
    emoji: String                        -- one of config.allowed_reactions
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- `issue` is blocked by `blocker` (and `blocker` is blocking `issue`).
-- from: models/issues/dependency.go:107
entity IssueDependency {
    issue: Issue
    blocker: Issue
    created_by: accounts/User
    created_at: Timestamp
}

-- Time a user spent on an issue. Deleting time hides it but keeps the record.
-- from: models/issues/tracked_time.go:23
entity TrackedTime {
    issue: Issue
    user: accounts/User                  -- whose time it is
    logged_by: accounts/User             -- who recorded it (decided: differs from `user`
                                         -- when a repository admin logs time for someone)
    amount: Duration
    created_at: Timestamp                -- the date the time is booked on
    is_deleted: Boolean
}

-- A running timer. A user has at most one running stopwatch at a time.
-- from: models/issues/stopwatch.go:33
entity Stopwatch {
    user: accounts/User
    issue: Issue
    started_at: Timestamp

    elapsed: now - started_at
}

-- An explicit subscription choice for one user on one issue. Absent a
-- choice, a user is subscribed when they watch the repository's issues or
-- participated (posted or commented).
-- from: models/issues/issue_watch.go:16
entity IssueWatch {
    user: accounts/User
    issue: Issue
    is_watching: Boolean
    updated_at: Timestamp
}

-- A pinned issue or PR; positions run 1..n per (repository, is_pull).
-- from: models/issues/issue.go:773
entity IssuePin {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    issue: Issue
    is_pull: Boolean
    position: Integer
}

-- A file attached to an issue, a comment or a release. An uploaded file
-- that is not linked yet is visible only to its uploader, and expires after
-- `orphan_attachment_expiry` (OrphanUploadExpires).
-- from: models/repo/attachment.go:23
entity Attachment {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    uploader: accounts/User
    name: String
    size: Integer                        -- bytes
    issue: Issue?
    comment: Comment?
    release: releases/Release?
    external_url: String?                -- release assets only (owned by releases)
    download_count: Integer              -- counted for release attachments only
    created_at: Timestamp

    is_linked: issue != null or release != null
}

-- One retained revision of an issue body (comment absent) or a comment.
-- from: models/issues/content_history.go:17
entity ContentHistory {
    issue: Issue
    comment: Comment?
    editor: accounts/User
    edited_at: Timestamp
    content: String
    is_first_created: Boolean
    is_deleted: Boolean                  -- soft-deleted revisions have their text erased
}

-- An issue template found on the repository's default branch.
-- from: modules/structs/issue.go:190
entity IssueTemplate {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    file_name: String
    format: TemplateFormat
    name: String                         -- required
    about: String                        -- required
    title: String?                       -- prefilled issue title
    labels: Set<String>                  -- label names applied when the issue is opened
    ref: String?
    body: String?                        -- markdown templates
    fields: List<IssueFormField>         -- yaml forms, at least one

    is_valid: template_is_valid(this)
}

-- The template chooser configuration on the default branch.
-- from: services/issue/template.go:58
entity IssueTemplateConfig {
    repository: repositories/Repository
    blank_issues_enabled: Boolean
    contact_links: List<ContactLink>
}

-- A named set of labels an instance offers for initialising a repository or
-- organization's labels.
-- from: modules/repository/init.go:146
entity LabelTemplate {
    name: String
    description: String
    labels: List<LabelSpec>
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- [attachment]
    attachments_enabled: Boolean = true
    attachment_allowed_types: String = ".avif,.cpuprofile,.csv,.dmp,.docx,.fodg,.fodp,.fods,.fodt,.gif,.gz,.jpeg,.jpg,.json,.jsonc,.log,.md,.mov,.mp4,.odf,.odg,.odp,.ods,.odt,.patch,.pdf,.png,.pptx,.svg,.tgz,.txt,.webm,.webp,.xls,.xlsx,.zip"
    attachment_max_size_mb: Integer = 2048
    attachment_max_files: Integer = 5
    orphan_attachment_expiry: Duration = 24.hours   -- decided: unlinked uploads expire

    -- [repository.issue]
    lock_reasons: Set<String> = { "Too heated", "Off-topic", "Spam", "Resolved" }
    max_pinned: Integer = 3                       -- 0 disables pinning

    -- [repository.pull-request] (keywords also apply to commit messages)
    close_keywords: Set<String> = { "close", "closes", "closed", "fix", "fixes", "fixed", "resolve", "resolves", "resolved" }
    reopen_keywords: Set<String> = { "reopen", "reopens", "reopened" }

    -- [ui]
    allowed_reactions: Set<String> = { "+1", "-1", "laugh", "hooray", "confused", "heart", "rocket", "eyes" }
    reaction_max_user_num: Integer = 10           -- names listed per reaction before "and N more"

    -- [service]
    timetracking_enabled: Boolean = true          -- instance switch; off hides all time tracking
    default_enable_timetracking: Boolean = true
    default_allow_only_contributors_to_track_time: Boolean = true
    default_enable_dependencies: Boolean = true
    allow_cross_repository_dependencies: Boolean = true

    -- Domain limits (not configurable in Forgejo)
    max_title_length: Integer = 255
    max_label_name_length: Integer = 50
    max_label_description_length: Integer = 200
    max_milestone_name_length: Integer = 50
    content_history_limit: Integer = 20
    max_manual_time: Duration = 1000.hours
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Defaults
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: options/label/Default
default LabelTemplate default_labels = {
    name: "Default",
    description: "Bug, enhancement, duplicate, invalid, question, wontfix and friends",
    labels: []
}

-- from: options/label/Advanced.yaml
default LabelTemplate advanced_labels = {
    name: "Advanced",
    description: "Scoped labels (Kind/, Priority/, Reviewed/, Status/) with exclusive scopes",
    labels: []
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: opening and editing issues
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Metadata (labels, milestone, assignees, due date, project) is only applied
-- when the poster can manage the tracker; for anyone else all of it is
-- silently dropped, on every path.
-- decided: all metadata from someone who cannot triage is dropped (the web form no longer keeps milestone / assignees)
-- Labels outside the repository / its organization are dropped; of several
-- labels in one exclusive scope only the last is kept.
-- `template` is the issue template the issue was opened from (null for a
-- blank issue). When the repository's template config sets
-- `blank_issues_enabled` to false, blank issues are refused on every path
-- (web form and API) except for repository writers.
-- decided: blank issues are refused when disabled, repository writers excepted
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:31
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue.go:1033 (chooser redirect when blank issues are disabled)
rule UserOpensIssue {
    when: UserOpensIssue(user, repository, title, content, labels, milestone, assignees, deadline, project, attachments, template)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(repository, user)
    requires: trim(title) != ""
    requires: length(title) <= config.max_title_length
    requires: milestone = null or milestone in (Milestones where repository = repository)
    requires: all_assignable(assignees, repository)        -- every one satisfies can_be_assigned
    requires: template = null or template.repository = repository
    let is_manager = can_manage_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: template != null or is_manager
              or not exists IssueTemplateConfig{repository: repository, blank_issues_enabled: false}
    let mentions = resolve_mentions_in(repository, user, content)
    ensures:
        let issue = Issue.created(
            repository: repository,
            index: next_issue_index(repository),
            poster: user,
            title: trim(title),
            content: content,
            content_version: 0,
            is_pull: false,
            status: open,
            is_locked: false,
            labels: if is_manager: without_scope_duplicates(labels_usable_in(labels, repository)) else: {},
            milestone: if is_manager: milestone else: null,
            assignees: if is_manager: assignees else: {},
            deadline: if is_manager: deadline else: null,
            mentioned_users: mentions,
            created_at: now,
            updated_at: now
        )
        IssueOpened(issue: issue, mentions: mentions)
        TextPosted(issue: issue, comment: null, doer: user, title: title, text: content)
        AttachmentsLinked(issue: issue, comment: null, doer: user, attachments: attachments)
        if is_manager:
            IssueMetadataInitialised(issue: issue, doer: user)
        -- decided (projects 4, 7): only an open board, and an organization board
        -- only for a poster who can write the organization's projects unit (triage
        -- on the issue is is_manager); otherwise the chosen board is dropped like
        -- the rest of the metadata of someone who may not set it
        if is_manager and project != null and project.status = open
           and (project.owner_kind != organization or can_write_org_projects(user, project.owner_org)):
            IssueCreatedWithProject(issue: issue, poster: user, project: project)
}

-- The timeline records the metadata chosen at creation as ordinary events.
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:357
rule RecordInitialMetadata {
    when: IssueMetadataInitialised(issue, doer)
    ensures:
        for l in issue.labels:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: doer, kind: label, label: l, label_added: true,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        if issue.milestone != null:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: doer, kind: milestone, new_milestone: issue.milestone,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        for a in issue.assignees:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: doer, kind: assignees, assignee: a, assignee_removed: false,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueLabelsChanged(issue: issue, doer: doer, added: issue.labels, removed: {})
}

-- The poster or a triager may change the title, also while the issue is
-- locked, on every path (the API's refusal of poster edits on a locked issue
-- is not kept for the title and description).
-- decided: a locked issue's poster may still correct its title and description; locking stops the conversation, not corrections
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:64
rule UserChangesIssueTitle {
    when: UserChangesIssueTitle(user, issue, title)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: user = issue.poster or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: not is_blocked(issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(issue.repository, user)
    requires: trim(title) != ""
    requires: length(title) <= config.max_title_length
    requires: trim(title) != issue.title
    ensures: issue.title = trim(title)
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: change_title,
                             old_title: issue.title, new_title: trim(title),
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: IssueTitleChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, old_title: issue.title)
    ensures: TextPosted(issue: issue, comment: null, doer: user, title: trim(title), text: issue.content)
}

-- Body edits are optimistic: the editor states the version they edited.
-- The first edit also records the original body as the first revision.
-- The poster may edit the body of a locked issue too.
-- decided: a locked issue's poster may still correct its title and description
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:257
rule UserEditsIssueBody {
    when: UserEditsIssueBody(user, issue, content, seen_version)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: user = issue.poster or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: seen_version = issue.content_version
    ensures: issue.content = content
    ensures: issue.content_version = issue.content_version + 1
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
    ensures: ContentRevised(issue: issue, comment: null, editor: user, old_content: issue.content, new_content: content)
    ensures: IssueContentChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, old_content: issue.content)
    ensures: TextPosted(issue: issue, comment: null, doer: user, title: issue.title, text: content)
}

-- Issues only: the branch or tag an issue is about. A set ref limits which
-- branch's commits may close the issue by keyword. On a locked issue only
-- triagers change it.
-- decided: on a locked issue the poster keeps only title and description edits; triagers may edit everything
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:105
-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_edit_issue.go:42 (poster edits refused while locked)
rule UserChangesIssueRef {
    when: UserChangesIssueRef(user, issue, ref)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: not issue.is_pull
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: user = issue.poster or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.is_locked or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: issue.ref = ref
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: change_issue_ref,
                             old_ref: issue.ref, new_ref: ref,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: IssueRefChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, old_ref: issue.ref)
}

-- The due date is a calendar day; it ends at the end of that day.
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:459
rule TriagerSetsDueDate {
    when: TriagerSetsDueDate(user, issue, deadline)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: deadline != issue.deadline
    ensures: issue.deadline = end_of_day(deadline)
    ensures:
        if issue.deadline = null:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: added_deadline, content: format_date(deadline),
                            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        else:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: modified_deadline, content: format_date(deadline),
                            content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:459
rule TriagerRemovesDueDate {
    when: TriagerRemovesDueDate(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: issue.deadline != null
    ensures: issue.deadline = null
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: removed_deadline, content: "",
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: closing, reopening, deleting
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The poster or a triager closes. With dependencies enabled, an issue with
-- open blockers cannot be closed (and the closer's stopwatch keeps running).
-- Closing stops the closer's own stopwatch on the issue. Pull requests are
-- closed and reopened through pulls, with the same permission and blocker
-- checks plus their own. On a locked issue only triagers change the state.
-- decided: on a locked issue the poster keeps only title and description edits; triagers may edit everything
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:69
-- from: routers/api/v1/permissions/req_edit_issue.go:42 (poster edits refused while locked)
rule UserClosesIssue {
    when: UserClosesIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: not issue.is_pull                 -- PRs: pulls/UserClosesPullRequest
    requires: issue.status = open
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: user = issue.poster or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.is_locked or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: not is_blocked(issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(issue.repository, user)
    requires: not (dependencies_enabled(issue.repository) and issue.has_open_blockers)
    ensures: issue.status = closed
    ensures: issue.closed_at = now
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
    ensures:
        let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: close, content: "",
                                content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueClosed(issue: issue, doer: user, comment: c)
    ensures:
        for sw in issue.stopwatches where user = user:
            StopwatchFinished(stopwatch: sw)
}

-- Reopening is never blocked by dependencies. On a locked issue only
-- triagers reopen.
-- decided: on a locked issue the poster keeps only title and description edits; triagers may edit everything
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:46
rule UserReopensIssue {
    when: UserReopensIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: not issue.is_pull                 -- PRs: pulls/UserReopensPullRequest
    requires: issue.status = closed
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: user = issue.poster or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.is_locked or can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: not is_blocked(issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(issue.repository, user)
    ensures: issue.status = open
    ensures: issue.closed_at = null
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
    ensures:
        let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: reopen, content: "",
                                content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueReopened(issue: issue, doer: user, comment: c)
}

-- Deleting removes the issue with its whole timeline, labels links,
-- dependencies (both directions), times, stopwatches, watches, reactions,
-- pin, attachments (files too), and references pointing from it.
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:171
rule RepoAdminDeletesIssue {
    when: RepoAdminDeletesIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, issue.repository)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: IssueRemoved(issue: issue, doer: user)
}

-- The removal itself, whoever asked for it (a repository admin, a site admin
-- acting on an abuse report, an account purge). `doer` is null for a purge.
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:171
rule RemoveIssue {
    when: IssueRemoved(issue, doer)
    ensures:
        for c in issue.comments:
            not exists c
        for r in issue.reactions:
            not exists r
        for d in issue.blocked_by:
            not exists d
        for d in issue.blocking:
            not exists d
        for t in issue.tracked_times:
            not exists t
        for sw in issue.stopwatches:
            not exists sw
        for w in issue.watches:
            not exists w
        for a in issue.attachments:
            not exists a
        for h in issue.history:
            not exists h
        for p in issue.pin:
            PinRemoved(pin: p)
        for c in Comments where ref_issue = issue:
            not exists c
        for c in Comments where dependent_issue = issue:
            not exists c
        not exists issue
        IssueDeleted(issue: issue, doer: doer)
}

-- A site admin deletes a reported issue or pull-request conversation from the
-- moderation queue (moderation has already checked the admin and the report).
-- from: routers/web/admin/reports.go:368
rule ModeratorRemovesIssue {
    when: moderation/ModeratorDeletesIssue(admin, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    ensures: IssueRemoved(issue: issue, doer: admin)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: the comment timeline
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An empty comment is allowed when it carries attachments. A comment may
-- carry a close / reopen request, which is processed as UserClosesIssue /
-- UserReopensIssue after the comment is posted.
-- from: services/issue/comments.go:49
rule UserComments {
    when: UserComments(user, issue, content, attachments)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: not issue.is_locked or can_triage(user, issue) or user.is_admin
    requires: not is_blocked(issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(issue.repository, user)
    requires: content != "" or attachments.count > 0
    let mentions = resolve_mentions(issue, user, content)
    ensures:
        let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: comment, content: content,
                                content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        AttachmentsLinked(issue: issue, comment: c, doer: user, attachments: attachments)
        TextPosted(issue: issue, comment: c, doer: user, title: null, text: content)
        IssueCommentCreated(issue: issue, comment: c, doer: user, mentions: mentions)
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
}

-- Only content-bearing kinds can be edited; edits are optimistic and keep
-- history (pending-review comments keep no history and notify nobody).
-- from: services/issue/comments.go:78
rule UserEditsComment {
    when: UserEditsComment(user, issue, comment, content, seen_version)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: comment.issue = issue
    requires: comment.has_content
    requires: can_read_issue(user, comment.issue)
    requires: user = comment.poster or can_triage(user, comment.issue)
    requires: not comment.issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: seen_version = comment.content_version
    ensures: comment.content = content
    ensures: comment.content_version = comment.content_version + 1
    ensures: comment.updated_at = now
    ensures: ContentRevised(issue: comment.issue, comment: comment, editor: user, old_content: comment.content, new_content: content)
    ensures: TextPosted(issue: comment.issue, comment: comment, doer: user, title: null, text: content)
    ensures: IssueCommentEdited(comment: comment, doer: user, old_content: comment.content)
}

-- Deleting a comment removes its reactions and history and neuters the
-- references it made.
-- from: models/issues/comment.go:1394
rule UserDeletesComment {
    when: UserDeletesComment(user, issue, comment)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: comment.issue = issue
    requires: comment.has_content
    requires: can_read_issue(user, comment.issue)
    requires: user = comment.poster or can_triage(user, comment.issue)
    requires: not comment.issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: CommentRemoved(comment: comment, doer: user)
}

-- The removal itself (by its poster or a triager, a site admin acting on an
-- abuse report, or an account deletion that removes contributions; `doer` is
-- null for the last).
-- from: models/issues/comment.go:1394
rule RemoveComment {
    when: CommentRemoved(comment, doer)
    -- the event carries the issue: listeners must not read it through the
    -- comment, which no longer exists once it is delivered
    let issue = comment.issue
    ensures:
        for r in comment.reactions:
            not exists r
        for h in comment.history:
            not exists h
        for x in Comments where ref_comment = comment and ref_action != neutered:
            x.ref_action = neutered
        not exists comment
        IssueCommentDeleted(comment: comment, issue: issue, doer: doer)
}

-- A site admin deletes a reported comment from the moderation queue.
-- from: routers/web/admin/reports.go:386
rule ModeratorRemovesComment {
    when: moderation/ModeratorDeletesComment(admin, comment)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    ensures: CommentRemoved(comment: comment, doer: admin)
}

-- A reply to a conversation mail becomes a plain comment by the token holder
-- (notifications has checked the token, read access and the lock). A reply to
-- a code comment (replied_to_code set) is pulls'. The mail's attachments
-- (attachment_count of them) are stored as this comment's attachments when
-- config.attachments_enabled and each is of an allowed type, like a web upload.
-- from: services/mailer/incoming/incoming_handler.go:150
rule CommentFromMailReply {
    when: notifications/MailReplyReceived(author, issue, replied_to, replied_to_code, body, attachment_count)
    requires: replied_to_code = null
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    -- the comment checks (archived repository, lock, blocks) are notifications'
    -- can_comment_on_issue, checked before it raised the reply (AcceptReplyByMail)
    let mentions = resolve_mentions(issue, author, body)
    ensures:
        let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: author, kind: comment, content: body,
                                content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        TextPosted(issue: issue, comment: c, doer: author, title: null, text: body)
        IssueCommentCreated(issue: issue, comment: c, doer: author, mentions: mentions)
    ensures: issue.updated_at = now
}

-- Mailing the unsubscribe address records an explicit unsubscribe.
-- from: services/mailer/incoming/incoming_handler.go:178
rule UnsubscribeByMail {
    when: notifications/MailUnsubscribeReceived(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    ensures:
        if exists IssueWatch{user: user, issue: issue}:
            IssueWatch{user: user, issue: issue}.is_watching = false
        else:
            IssueWatch.created(user: user, issue: issue, is_watching: false, updated_at: now)
}

-- Content history: the first edit records the original text as the first
-- revision, every edit records the new text. Only `content_history_limit`
-- revisions are kept; when over, the revision closest in time to its
-- predecessor is dropped (never the first or the latest).
-- from: models/issues/content_history.go:41
rule RecordContentRevision {
    when: ContentRevised(issue, comment, editor, old_content, new_content)
    let existing = ContentHistories where issue = issue and comment = comment
    ensures:
        if existing.count = 0:
            ContentHistory.created(issue: issue, comment: comment, editor: original_author(issue, comment),
                                   edited_at: original_time(issue, comment), content: old_content,
                                   is_first_created: true, is_deleted: false)
        ContentHistory.created(issue: issue, comment: comment, editor: editor, edited_at: now,
                               content: new_content, is_first_created: false, is_deleted: false)
        if existing.count + 2 > config.content_history_limit:
            not exists closest_spaced_revision(existing)
}

-- Triagers and the repository owner can hide any revision; the issue /
-- comment author and the revision's author can hide their own.
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue_content_history.go:95
rule UserHidesContentRevision {
    when: UserHidesContentRevision(user, issue, revision)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: revision.issue = issue
    requires: can_read_issue(user, revision.issue)
    requires: not revision.issue.repository.is_archived
    requires:
        can_triage(user, revision.issue)
        or user = revision.editor
        or (revision.comment = null and user = revision.issue.poster)
        or (revision.comment != null and user = revision.comment.poster)
    ensures: revision.is_deleted = true
    ensures: revision.content = ""
}

-- Mentions in posted text (a body or a comment, never a title) are recorded for the issue.
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:484
rule RecordMentions {
    when: TextPosted(issue, comment, doer, title, text)
    ensures: issue.mentioned_users = issue.mentioned_users + resolve_mentions(issue, doer, text)
}

-- Opening the issue page records that the viewer has read it (notifications
-- marks the matching inbox thread read).
-- from: models/issues/issue_user.go:60
rule UserViewsIssue {
    when: UserViewsIssue(viewer, issue)
    requires: can_read_issue(viewer, issue)
    ensures: issue.read_by = issue.read_by + { viewer }
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: cross references
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Text of an issue / PR (title + body) or of a comment that references other
-- issues leaves a reference entry on each target's timeline. Re-posting
-- (an edit) neuters references that disappeared and adds new ones; an
-- unchanged reference is left as it is. Self references are ignored.
-- from: models/issues/issue_xref.go:71
rule RecordCrossReferences {
    when: TextPosted(issue, comment, doer, title, text)
    let found = cross_references(issue.repository, doer, title, text)
    let previous = Comments where ref_issue = issue and ref_comment = comment and ref_action != neutered
    ensures:
        for old in previous:
            if not still_referenced(old, found):
                old.ref_action = neutered
        for x in found where x.target != issue:
            if not already_recorded(x, previous):
                Comment.created(
                    issue: x.target,
                    poster: doer,
                    kind: if comment != null: comment_ref else if issue.is_pull: pull_ref else: issue_ref,
                    ref_issue: issue,
                    ref_comment: comment,
                    ref_action: x.action,
                    content: "",
                    content_version: 0,
                    created_at: now,
                    updated_at: now
                )
}

-- Merging closes the PR's conversation (pulls); the merger's own stopwatch on
-- it stops like on any close.
-- from: services/issue/status.go:31
rule MergerStopwatchStops {
    when: pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger)
    ensures:
        for sw in Stopwatches where user = merger and issue = pull_request.issue:
            StopwatchFinished(stopwatch: sw)
}

-- A merged PR applies the latest closing / reopening reference it made to
-- each issue (pulls decides which issues; see pulls/MergeClosesReferencedIssues).
-- from: services/pull/merge.go:288
rule MergeClosesReferencedIssue {
    when: pulls/IssueClosedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer)
    ensures: ReferenceResolved(issue: issue, doer: doer, closing: true)
}

-- from: services/pull/merge.go:288
rule MergeReopensReferencedIssue {
    when: pulls/IssueReopenedByPullRequest(issue, pull_request, doer)
    ensures: ReferenceResolved(issue: issue, doer: doer, closing: false)
}


-- Applying a resolved close / reopen reference (from a merged PR or a pushed
-- commit). An issue with open blockers is left open: the failure is
-- swallowed, not reported.
-- from: services/pull/merge.go:299
rule ApplyResolvedReference {
    when: ReferenceResolved(issue, doer, closing)
    requires: (closing and issue.status = open) or (not closing and issue.status = closed)
    requires: not (closing and dependencies_enabled(issue.repository) and issue.has_open_blockers)
    ensures:
        if closing:
            issue.status = closed
            issue.closed_at = now
            let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: doer, kind: close, content: "",
                                    content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
            IssueClosed(issue: issue, doer: doer, comment: c)
            for sw in issue.stopwatches where user = doer:
                StopwatchFinished(stopwatch: sw)
        else:
            issue.status = open
            issue.closed_at = null
            let r = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: doer, kind: reopen, content: "",
                                    content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
            IssueReopened(issue: issue, doer: doer, comment: r)
}


-- Commit messages pushed to a repository reference issues (same repository
-- or `owner/repo#N`). Every reference the pusher can read leaves one
-- `commit_ref` entry per commit; a close / reopen keyword acts on an issue
-- (never a PR) when the pusher could close it manually and the commit is on
-- the issue's ref branch, else on the default branch, unless the repository
-- closes via commits in any branch. `Fixes #1 @1h30m` also logs the time.
-- A deploy-key push (push.pusher null, decided code 4) references nothing:
-- no reference is attributed to a user.
-- from: services/issue/commit.go:106
rule PushedCommitReferencesIssue {
    when: code/PushReceived(push)
    for ref in commit_references(push) where push.pusher != null and can_read_issue(push.pusher, ref.target):
        let target = ref.target
        let pusher = push.pusher
        ensures:
            if not exists Comment{issue: target, kind: commit_ref, commit_sha: ref.commit_sha}:
                Comment.created(issue: target, poster: pusher, kind: commit_ref, commit_sha: ref.commit_sha,
                                content: ref.commit_message, content_version: 0,
                                created_at: now, updated_at: now)
                IssueReferencedByCommit(issue: target, commit_sha: ref.commit_sha, pusher: pusher)
            if ref.action != none
               and not target.is_pull
               and (pusher = target.poster or can_triage(pusher, target))
               and branch_may_close(target, push.repository, ref.branch):
                if ref.action = closes and ref.time_log != null:
                    TimeLogged(user: pusher, issue: target, amount: ref.time_log, at: ref.committed_at, logged_by: pusher)
                ReferenceResolved(issue: target, doer: pusher, closing: ref.action = closes)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: locking and pinning
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A locked conversation accepts comments only from triagers and site admins;
-- reactions stay open to every reader. The reason must be empty or one of
-- the configured lock reasons, on every path (web and API).
-- decided: lock reasons are validated on every path: empty or one of config.lock_reasons
-- from: models/issues/issue_lock.go:22
-- from: routers/web/repo/issue_lock.go:27 (reason validated against LOCK_REASONS)
rule TriagerLocksIssue {
    when: TriagerLocksIssue(user, issue, reason)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: not issue.is_locked
    requires: reason = "" or is_lock_reason(reason)      -- reason in config.lock_reasons
    ensures: issue.is_locked = true
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: lock, content: reason,
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/issue_lock.go:27
rule TriagerUnlocksIssue {
    when: TriagerUnlocksIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: issue.is_locked
    ensures: issue.is_locked = false
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: unlock, content: "",
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- Issues and PRs have separate pin lists of at most `max_pinned` each.
-- from: models/issues/issue.go:773
rule RepoAdminPinsIssue {
    when: RepoAdminPinsIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, issue.repository)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: issue.pin.count = 0
    let pins = IssuePins where repository = issue.repository and is_pull = issue.is_pull
    requires: pins.count < config.max_pinned
    ensures: IssuePin.created(repository: issue.repository, issue: issue, is_pull: issue.is_pull, position: pins.count + 1)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: pin, content: "",
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/issue.go:814
rule RepoAdminUnpinsIssue {
    when: RepoAdminUnpinsIssue(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, issue.repository)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: issue.pin.count > 0
    ensures:
        for p in issue.pin:
            PinRemoved(pin: p)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: unpin, content: "",
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- Later pins move up to close the gap.
-- from: models/issues/issue.go:821
rule ClosePinGap {
    when: PinRemoved(pin)
    let later = IssuePins where repository = pin.repository and is_pull = pin.is_pull and position > pin.position
    ensures:
        for p in later:
            p.position = p.position - 1
        not exists pin
}

-- Positions beyond the end are clamped to the end.
-- from: models/issues/issue.go:859
rule RepoAdminMovesPin {
    when: RepoAdminMovesPin(user, repository, pin, position)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: pin.repository = repository
    requires: is_repo_admin(user, pin.repository)
    requires: not pin.repository.is_archived
    requires: position >= 1
    let siblings = IssuePins where repository = pin.repository and is_pull = pin.is_pull
    ensures: pin.position = min_of(position, siblings.count)
    ensures:
        for p in siblings:
            if p != pin:
                p.position = shifted_position(p.position, pin.position, min_of(position, siblings.count))
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: labels
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/issues/label.go:207
rule TrackerManagerCreatesLabel {
    when: TrackerManagerCreatesLabel(user, repository, name, description, color, is_exclusive)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(name) <= config.max_label_name_length
    requires: length(description) <= config.max_label_description_length
    requires: is_valid_color(color)
    ensures: Label.created(repository: repository, name: name, description: description,
                           color: normalize_color(color), is_exclusive: is_exclusive, created_at: now)
}

-- Archiving keeps the label on its issues but hides it from the label filter
-- and marks it in pickers.
-- from: models/issues/label.go:240
rule TrackerManagerEditsLabel {
    when: TrackerManagerEditsLabel(user, repository, label, name, description, color, is_exclusive, is_archived)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: label.repository = repository
    requires: label.repository != null
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, label.repository)
    requires: not label.repository.is_archived
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(name) <= config.max_label_name_length
    requires: length(description) <= config.max_label_description_length
    requires: is_valid_color(color)
    ensures: label.name = name
    ensures: label.description = description
    ensures: label.color = normalize_color(color)
    ensures: label.is_exclusive = is_exclusive
    ensures:
        if is_archived and label.archived_at = null:
            label.archived_at = now
        if not is_archived:
            label.archived_at = null
}

-- Deleting a label removes it from all issues; its timeline events stay
-- (see RemoveLabelEverywhere).
-- from: models/issues/label.go:292
rule TrackerManagerDeletesLabel {
    when: TrackerManagerDeletesLabel(user, repository, label)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: label.repository = repository
    requires: label.repository != null
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, label.repository)
    requires: not label.repository.is_archived
    ensures: LabelRemovedEverywhere(doomed: label)
}

-- from: models/issues/label.go:207
rule OrgOwnerCreatesLabel {
    when: OrgOwnerCreatesLabel(user, organization, name, description, color, is_exclusive)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: is_org_owner(organization, user)
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(name) <= config.max_label_name_length
    requires: length(description) <= config.max_label_description_length
    requires: is_valid_color(color)
    ensures: Label.created(organization: organization, name: name, description: description,
                           color: normalize_color(color), is_exclusive: is_exclusive, created_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/label.go:240
rule OrgOwnerEditsLabel {
    when: OrgOwnerEditsLabel(user, organization, label, name, description, color, is_exclusive, is_archived)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: label.organization = organization
    requires: label.organization != null
    requires: is_org_owner(label.organization, user)
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(name) <= config.max_label_name_length
    requires: is_valid_color(color)
    ensures: label.name = name
    ensures: label.description = description
    ensures: label.color = normalize_color(color)
    ensures: label.is_exclusive = is_exclusive
    ensures:
        if is_archived and label.archived_at = null:
            label.archived_at = now
        if not is_archived:
            label.archived_at = null
}

-- from: models/issues/label.go:258
rule OrgOwnerDeletesLabel {
    when: OrgOwnerDeletesLabel(user, organization, label)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: label.organization = organization
    requires: label.organization != null
    requires: is_org_owner(label.organization, user)
    ensures: LabelRemovedEverywhere(doomed: label)
}

-- The label's timeline events are kept, showing the label's name and marked
-- deleted (Forgejo erases them; milestones already kept theirs).
-- decided: timeline events of deleted labels and milestones are kept for both, showing the name, marked deleted
-- from: models/issues/label.go:292
rule RemoveLabelEverywhere {
    when: LabelRemovedEverywhere(doomed)
    let doomed_name = doomed.name
    ensures:
        for i in Issues where doomed in labels:
            i.labels = i.labels - { doomed }
        for c in Comments where label = doomed:
            c.deleted_label_name = doomed_name
            c.label = null
        not exists doomed
}

-- Adds every label of the chosen template to the repository (or, from the
-- organization settings, to the organization).
-- from: modules/repository/init.go:146
rule TrackerManagerInitialisesLabels {
    when: TrackerManagerInitialisesLabels(user, repository, template)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    ensures:
        for spec in template.labels:
            Label.created(repository: repository, name: spec.name, description: spec.description ?? "",
                          color: normalize_color(spec.color), is_exclusive: spec.is_exclusive, created_at: now)
}

-- from: routers/web/org/org_labels.go:1
rule OrgOwnerInitialisesLabels {
    when: OrgOwnerInitialisesLabels(user, organization, template)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: is_org_owner(organization, user)
    ensures:
        for spec in template.labels:
            Label.created(organization: organization, name: spec.name, description: spec.description ?? "",
                          color: normalize_color(spec.color), is_exclusive: spec.is_exclusive, created_at: now)
}

-- Adding a label in an exclusive scope removes the issue's other labels in
-- that scope. Labels from outside the repository / its organization are
-- ignored.
-- from: models/issues/issue_label.go:89
rule TriagerAddsLabel {
    when: TriagerAddsLabel(user, issue, added)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: added not in issue.labels
    requires: added.repository = issue.repository or added.organization = issue.repository.owner_org
    let displaced = issue.labels where scope = added.scope and scope != "" and is_exclusive
    ensures: issue.labels = issue.labels - displaced + { added }
    ensures:
        for d in displaced:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: d, label_added: false,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: added, label_added: true,
                        content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueLabelsChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, added: { added }, removed: displaced)
}

-- from: services/issue/label.go:47
rule TriagerRemovesLabel {
    when: TriagerRemovesLabel(user, issue, removed)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: removed in issue.labels
    ensures: issue.labels = issue.labels - { removed }
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: removed, label_added: false,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: IssueLabelsChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, added: {}, removed: { removed })
}

-- Replace the whole label set (API PUT / web multi-select).
-- from: models/issues/issue_label.go:447
rule TriagerReplacesLabels {
    when: TriagerReplacesLabels(user, issue, labels)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    let wanted = without_scope_duplicates(labels_usable_in(labels, issue.repository))
    ensures: issue.labels = wanted
    ensures:
        for l in wanted - issue.labels:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: l, label_added: true,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        for l in issue.labels - wanted:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: l, label_added: false,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueLabelsChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, added: wanted - issue.labels, removed: issue.labels - wanted)
}

-- from: models/issues/issue_label.go:374
rule TriagerClearsLabels {
    when: TriagerClearsLabels(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: issue.labels = {}
    ensures:
        for l in issue.labels:
            Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: label, label: l, label_added: false,
                            content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueLabelsCleared(issue: issue, doer: user)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: milestones
------------------------------------------------------------

-- An empty due date means none.
-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:116
rule TrackerManagerCreatesMilestone {
    when: TrackerManagerCreatesMilestone(user, repository, name, description, deadline)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(trim(name)) <= config.max_milestone_name_length
    ensures: Milestone.created(repository: repository, name: trim(name), description: description,
                               status: open, deadline: deadline, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:166
rule TrackerManagerEditsMilestone {
    when: TrackerManagerEditsMilestone(user, repository, milestone, name, description, deadline)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: milestone.repository = repository
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, milestone.repository)
    requires: not milestone.repository.is_archived
    requires: trim(name) != "" and length(trim(name)) <= config.max_milestone_name_length
    ensures: milestone.name = trim(name)
    ensures: milestone.description = description
    ensures: milestone.deadline = deadline
    ensures: milestone.updated_at = now
}

-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:228
rule TrackerManagerClosesMilestone {
    when: TrackerManagerClosesMilestone(user, repository, milestone)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: milestone.repository = repository
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, milestone.repository)
    requires: not milestone.repository.is_archived
    requires: milestone.status = open
    ensures: milestone.status = closed
    ensures: milestone.closed_at = now
}

-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:228
rule TrackerManagerReopensMilestone {
    when: TrackerManagerReopensMilestone(user, repository, milestone)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: milestone.repository = repository
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, milestone.repository)
    requires: not milestone.repository.is_archived
    requires: milestone.status = closed
    ensures: milestone.status = open
    ensures: milestone.closed_at = null
}

-- Issues of a deleted milestone keep no milestone; their timeline events
-- stay, showing the milestone's name, marked deleted.
-- decided: timeline events of deleted labels and milestones are kept for both, showing the name, marked deleted
-- from: models/issues/milestone.go:245
rule TrackerManagerDeletesMilestone {
    when: TrackerManagerDeletesMilestone(user, repository, milestone)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: milestone.repository = repository
    requires: can_manage_tracker(user, milestone.repository)
    requires: not milestone.repository.is_archived
    let milestone_name = milestone.name
    ensures:
        for i in milestone.issues:
            i.milestone = null
        for c in Comments where old_milestone = milestone:
            c.deleted_old_milestone_name = milestone_name
            c.old_milestone = null
        for c in Comments where new_milestone = milestone:
            c.deleted_new_milestone_name = milestone_name
            c.new_milestone = null
        not exists milestone
}

-- Setting none (null) removes the milestone. Applies to a batch of issues
-- in the web UI.
-- from: services/issue/milestone.go:91
rule TriagerSetsMilestone {
    when: TriagerSetsMilestone(user, issue, target)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: target = null or target in (Milestones where repository = issue.repository)
    requires: target != issue.milestone
    ensures: issue.milestone = target
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: milestone,
                             old_milestone: issue.milestone, new_milestone: target,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: IssueMilestoneChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, old_milestone: issue.milestone)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: assignees
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Toggling: assigning an assigned user unassigns them.
-- from: services/issue/assignee.go:47
rule TriagerTogglesAssignee {
    when: TriagerTogglesAssignee(user, issue, assignee)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: can_be_assigned(assignee, issue.repository)
    let removing = assignee in issue.assignees
    ensures:
        if removing:
            issue.assignees = issue.assignees - { assignee }
        else:
            issue.assignees = issue.assignees + { assignee }
    ensures:
        let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: assignees, assignee: assignee,
                                assignee_removed: removing, content: "", content_version: 0,
                                created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        IssueAssigneeChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, assignee: assignee, removed: removing, comment: c)
}

-- API semantics: the given set replaces the current assignees ([] clears).
-- from: services/issue/issue.go:124
rule TriagerReplacesAssignees {
    when: TriagerReplacesAssignees(user, issue, wanted)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: all_assignable(wanted, issue.repository)  -- every one satisfies can_be_assigned
    ensures: issue.assignees = wanted
    ensures:
        for a in issue.assignees - wanted:
            let c = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: assignees, assignee: a,
                                    assignee_removed: true, content: "", content_version: 0,
                                    created_at: now, updated_at: now)
            IssueAssigneeChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, assignee: a, removed: true, comment: c)
        for a in wanted - issue.assignees:
            let c2 = Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: assignees, assignee: a,
                                     assignee_removed: false, content: "", content_version: 0,
                                     created_at: now, updated_at: now)
            IssueAssigneeChanged(issue: issue, doer: user, assignee: a, removed: false, comment: c2)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: dependencies
------------------------------------------------------------

-- `issue` becomes blocked by `blocker`. Both issues' timelines record it.
-- from: models/issues/dependency.go:130
rule TriagerAddsDependency {
    when: TriagerAddsDependency(user, issue, blocker)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: dependencies_enabled(issue.repository)
    requires: can_triage(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: can_read_issue(user, blocker)
    requires: blocker != issue
    requires: blocker.repository = issue.repository or config.allow_cross_repository_dependencies
    requires: not exists IssueDependency{issue: issue, blocker: blocker}
    requires: not exists IssueDependency{issue: blocker, blocker: issue}
    ensures: IssueDependency.created(issue: issue, blocker: blocker, created_by: user, created_at: now)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: add_dependency, dependent_issue: blocker,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: blocker, poster: user, kind: add_dependency, dependent_issue: issue,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/dependency.go:171
rule TriagerRemovesDependency {
    when: TriagerRemovesDependency(user, issue, dependency)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: dependency.issue = issue
    requires: dependencies_enabled(dependency.issue.repository)
    requires: can_triage(user, dependency.issue)
    requires: not dependency.issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: dependency.issue, poster: user, kind: remove_dependency,
                             dependent_issue: dependency.blocker, content: "", content_version: 0,
                             created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: dependency.blocker, poster: user, kind: remove_dependency,
                             dependent_issue: dependency.issue, content: "", content_version: 0,
                             created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: not exists dependency
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: time tracking
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Starting a stopwatch finishes any other stopwatch the user has running.
-- from: models/issues/stopwatch.go:200
rule UserStartsStopwatch {
    when: UserStartsStopwatch(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: may_track_time(user, issue)
    requires: not exists Stopwatch{user: user, issue: issue}
    ensures:
        for other in Stopwatches where user = user:
            StopwatchFinished(stopwatch: other)
        Stopwatch.created(user: user, issue: issue, started_at: now)
        Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: start_tracking, content: "",
                        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- from: models/issues/stopwatch.go:154
rule UserStopsStopwatch {
    when: UserStopsStopwatch(user, issue, stopwatch)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: stopwatch.issue = issue
    requires: stopwatch.user = user
    requires: may_track_time(user, stopwatch.issue)
    ensures: StopwatchFinished(stopwatch: stopwatch)
}

-- The elapsed time becomes tracked time.
-- from: models/issues/stopwatch.go:154
rule FinishStopwatch {
    when: StopwatchFinished(stopwatch)
    -- read before the stopwatch goes (postconditions see the resulting state)
    let issue = stopwatch.issue
    let tracker = stopwatch.user
    let spent = now - stopwatch.started_at
    ensures:
        let t = TrackedTime.created(issue: issue, user: tracker, logged_by: tracker,
                                    amount: spent, created_at: now, is_deleted: false)
        Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: tracker, kind: stop_tracking, tracked_time: t,
                        content: format_duration(spent), content_version: 0,
                        created_at: now, updated_at: now)
        not exists stopwatch
}

-- from: models/issues/stopwatch.go:255
rule UserCancelsStopwatch {
    when: UserCancelsStopwatch(user, issue, stopwatch)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: stopwatch.issue = issue
    requires: stopwatch.user = user
    requires: may_track_time(user, stopwatch.issue)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: stopwatch.issue, poster: user, kind: cancel_tracking, content: "",
                             content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
    ensures: not exists stopwatch
}

-- Manual time: positive and at most `max_manual_time` per entry (web form:
-- hours and minutes each 0..1000).
-- from: models/issues/tracked_time.go:170
rule UserAddsTime {
    when: UserAddsTime(user, issue, amount)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: may_track_time(user, issue)
    requires: amount > 0.seconds
    requires: amount <= config.max_manual_time
    ensures: TimeLogged(user: user, issue: issue, amount: amount, at: now, logged_by: user)
}

-- A repository admin (site admins included) may log time for another user,
-- on a date they choose, on every path (web and API); the entry records who
-- logged it.
-- decided: repository admins may log time for someone else on every path, with a chosen date; the entry records who logged it
-- from: routers/api/v1/repo/issue_tracked_time.go:201
rule AdminAddsTimeForUser {
    when: AdminAddsTimeForUser(admin, issue, user, amount, at)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: may_track_time(admin, issue)
    requires: is_repo_admin(admin, issue.repository) or admin.is_admin
    requires: amount > 0.seconds
    requires: amount <= config.max_manual_time
    ensures: TimeLogged(user: user, issue: issue, amount: amount, at: at, logged_by: admin)
}

-- from: models/issues/tracked_time.go:170
rule LogTime {
    when: TimeLogged(user, issue, amount, at, logged_by)
    ensures:
        let t = TrackedTime.created(issue: issue, user: user, logged_by: logged_by, amount: amount,
                                    created_at: at, is_deleted: false)
        Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: add_time_manual, tracked_time: t,
                        content: format_duration(amount), content_version: 0,
                        created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- Only the user who tracked the time or a site admin deletes it.
-- from: models/issues/tracked_time.go:282
rule UserDeletesTime {
    when: UserDeletesTime(user, issue, time)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: time.issue = issue
    requires: may_track_time(user, time.issue)
    requires: time.user = user or user.is_admin
    requires: not time.is_deleted
    ensures: time.is_deleted = true
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: time.issue, poster: time.user, kind: delete_time_manual,
                             content: format_duration(time.amount), content_version: 0,
                             created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

-- API: delete all of one's own time on an issue.
-- from: models/issues/tracked_time.go:243
rule UserResetsOwnTime {
    when: UserResetsOwnTime(user, issue)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: may_track_time(user, issue)
    let mine = issue.tracked_times where user = user and is_deleted = false
    requires: mine.count > 0
    ensures:
        for t in mine:
            t.is_deleted = true
        Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: user, kind: delete_time_manual, content: "",
                        content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: reactions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user reacts at most once per emoji per target. The lock does not
-- affect reactions: anyone who can read may react on a locked issue.
-- decided: anyone who can read may react; the lock doesn't affect reactions (the API's write requirement is dropped)
-- from: services/issue/reaction.go:14
rule UserReactsToIssue {
    when: UserReactsToIssue(user, issue, emoji)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: not issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: is_allowed_reaction(emoji)               -- emoji in config.allowed_reactions
    requires: not is_blocked(issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(issue.repository, user)
    requires: not exists Reaction{user: user, issue: issue, comment: null, emoji: emoji}
    ensures:
        let r = Reaction.created(user: user, issue: issue, comment: null, emoji: emoji, created_at: now)
        ReactionAdded(reaction: r)
}

-- decided: anyone who can read may react; the lock doesn't affect reactions
-- from: services/issue/reaction.go:46
rule UserReactsToComment {
    when: UserReactsToComment(user, issue, comment, emoji)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: comment.issue = issue
    requires: comment.has_content
    requires: can_read_issue(user, comment.issue)
    requires: not comment.issue.repository.is_archived
    requires: is_allowed_reaction(emoji)               -- emoji in config.allowed_reactions
    requires: not is_blocked(comment.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked(comment.issue.poster, user)
    requires: not is_blocked_by_owner(comment.issue.repository, user)
    requires: not exists Reaction{user: user, issue: comment.issue, comment: comment, emoji: emoji}
    ensures:
        let r = Reaction.created(user: user, issue: comment.issue, comment: comment, emoji: emoji, created_at: now)
        ReactionAdded(reaction: r)
}

-- from: services/issue/reaction.go:36
rule UserRemovesReaction {
    when: UserRemovesReaction(user, issue, reaction)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: reaction.issue = issue
    requires: reaction.user = user
    requires: not reaction.issue.repository.is_archived
    ensures: ReactionRemoved(reaction: reaction)
    ensures: not exists reaction
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: subscriptions
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A user sets their own subscription; site admins may set anyone's (API).
-- from: models/issues/issue_watch.go:33
rule UserSetsIssueSubscription {
    when: UserSetsIssueSubscription(user, issue, subscriber, watching)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: can_read_issue(user, issue)
    requires: subscriber = user or user.is_admin
    ensures:
        if exists IssueWatch{user: subscriber, issue: issue}:
            IssueWatch{user: subscriber, issue: issue}.is_watching = watching
        else:
            IssueWatch.created(user: subscriber, issue: issue, is_watching: watching, updated_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: attachments
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Upload first, link later: the file belongs to the repository and its
-- uploader until it is linked to an issue or comment by posting / editing.
-- The type is checked against the file name and its leading bytes.
-- from: services/attachment/attachment.go:78
rule UserUploadsAttachment {
    when: UserUploadsAttachment(user, repository, name, size, head_bytes)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: config.attachments_enabled
    requires: can_read_tracker(user, repository)
    requires: not repository.is_archived
    requires: is_allowed_file(name, head_bytes)   -- against config.attachment_allowed_types
    requires: size <= config.attachment_max_size_mb * 1048576
    requires: attachment_quota_allows(repository, size)   -- decided (quota 2): usage + size <= limit
    ensures: Attachment.created(repository: repository, uploader: user, name: name, size: size,
                                issue: null, comment: null, release: null, external_url: null,
                                download_count: 0, created_at: now)
}

-- Posting or editing text links the listed uploads (same repository) to the
-- issue or comment; on edit, previously linked files not listed are removed.
-- At most `attachment_max_files` per upload batch.
-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:237
rule LinkAttachments {
    when: AttachmentsLinked(issue, comment, doer, attachments)
    requires: attachments.count <= config.attachment_max_files
    ensures:
        for a in attachments:
            if a.repository = issue.repository and not a.is_linked:
                a.issue = issue
                a.comment = comment
}

-- Uploads that are never linked to an issue, comment or release expire
-- after `orphan_attachment_expiry`. Forgejo keeps them indefinitely (only a
-- doctor check removes orphans); the sweep is administration's hourly
-- delete_orphaned_attachments task, which hands over that expiry.
-- decided: orphan uploads expire when unlinked within a configurable time (default 24 hours), via a scheduled task
-- from: models/repo/attachment.go:319 (DeleteOrphanedAttachments, doctor only)
rule OrphanUploadExpires {
    when: administration/OrphanedUploadCleanupDue(older_than)
    ensures:
        for upload in Attachments where issue = null and comment = null and release = null
                and created_at + older_than <= now:
            not exists upload
    ensures: OrphanedUploadCleanupFinished()   -- decided: requests 5 (the owner reports the run done)
}

-- The uploader removes their own upload (web); via the API whoever may edit
-- the issue / comment may remove or rename its attachments.
-- from: routers/web/repo/attachment.go:63
rule UserDeletesAttachment {
    when: UserDeletesAttachment(user, issue, attachment)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: attachment.issue = null or attachment.issue = issue   -- an upload not yet posted, or one on this issue
    requires: not attachment.repository.is_archived
    requires:
        user = attachment.uploader
        or (attachment.issue != null and attachment.comment = null
            and (user = attachment.issue.poster or can_triage(user, attachment.issue)))
        or (attachment.comment != null
            and (user = attachment.comment.poster or can_triage(user, attachment.issue)))
    ensures: not exists attachment
}

-- from: routers/api/v1/repo/issue_attachment.go:234
rule UserRenamesAttachment {
    when: UserRenamesAttachment(user, issue, attachment, name)
    requires: not (exists access/InstanceWriteGate{read_only: true})   -- decided: administration 3 (read-only mode refuses every write)
    requires: attachment.issue = issue
    requires: attachment.issue != null
    requires: not attachment.repository.is_archived
    requires: user = attachment.uploader or user = attachment.issue.poster or can_triage(user, attachment.issue)
    requires: is_allowed_file(name, "")
    ensures: attachment.name = name
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules: repository lifecycle
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/issues/issue_update.go:661
rule TrackerDeletedWithRepository {
    when: repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository, doer)
    ensures:
        for i in Issues where repository = repository:
            not exists i
        for l in Labels where repository = repository:
            not exists l
        for m in Milestones where repository = repository:
            not exists m
        for a in Attachments where repository = repository:
            not exists a
        for p in IssuePins where repository = repository:
            not exists p
}

-- A user who loses read access to a repository, for any reason, loses their issue
-- subscriptions there and every assignment in it they may no longer hold.
-- decided: access decision 7: subscriptions are cleared immediately on losing read access
-- from: models/org_team.go:538
rule ClearInvolvementOnLostAccess {
    when: access/UserLostRepositoryAccess(user, repository)
    ensures:
        for w in IssueWatches where w.user = user and w.issue.repository = repository:
            not exists w
        for i in Issues where i.repository = repository and user in i.assignees:
            if not can_be_assigned(user, repository):
                i.assignees = i.assignees - { user }
}

-- Removing a collaborator unassigns them from the repository's issues they
-- may no longer be assigned (they may keep access through a team).
-- from: models/repo/collaboration.go:98 (reconsiderRepoIssuesAssignee)
rule UnassignRemovedCollaborator {
    when: repositories/CollaboratorRemoved(repository, user, doer)
    ensures:
        for i in Issues where i.repository = repository and user in i.assignees:
            if not can_be_assigned(user, repository):
                i.assignees = i.assignees - { user }
}

-- A repository created with a label template gets that template's labels.
-- from: modules/repository/init.go:146
rule CreateLabelsFromTemplate {
    when: repositories/LabelTemplateApplied(repository, template_name)
    ensures:
        for t in LabelTemplates where name = template_name:
            for spec in t.labels:
                Label.created(repository: repository, name: spec.name, description: spec.description ?? "",
                              color: normalize_color(spec.color), is_exclusive: spec.is_exclusive, created_at: now)
}

-- A repository generated from a template with "labels" chosen gets a copy of
-- the template repository's own labels (archived ones stay archived).
-- from: services/repository/generate.go:61
rule CopyTemplateLabels {
    when: repositories/RepositoryGeneratedFromTemplate(template, repository, doer, git_content, topics, git_hooks, webhooks, avatar, labels, protected_branches)
    requires: labels
    ensures:
        for l in Labels where repository = template:
            Label.created(repository: repository, name: l.name, description: l.description, color: l.color,
                          is_exclusive: l.is_exclusive, archived_at: l.archived_at, created_at: now)
}

-- A deleted account leaves no reactions, stopwatches, subscriptions,
-- assignments or read markers; tracked time is kept (shown as the ghost
-- user). When contributions are deleted (purge, or a young account) its plain
-- comments go too, and a purge also removes every issue it opened (pull
-- request conversations go with their pull request, pulls'). Otherwise its
-- content stays and shows as the ghost user. `user` is already gone: only its
-- identity is compared.
-- from: services/user/delete.go:36
rule ClearTracesOfDeletedAccount {
    when: accounts/UserAccountDeleted(user, kind, purge, delete_contributions)
    ensures:
        for r in Reactions where r.user = user:
            not exists r
        for sw in Stopwatches where sw.user = user:
            not exists sw
        for w in IssueWatches where w.user = user:
            not exists w
        for i in Issues where user in i.assignees:
            i.assignees = i.assignees - { user }
        for i in Issues where user in i.read_by:
            i.read_by = i.read_by - { user }
    ensures:
        if delete_contributions:
            for c in Comments where c.poster = user and c.kind = comment:
                CommentRemoved(comment: c, doer: null)
    ensures:
        if purge:
            for i in Issues where i.poster = user and not i.is_pull:
                IssueRemoved(issue: i, doer: null)
}

-- Putting an issue on a board, moving it to another or taking it off leaves a
-- `project` entry on its timeline.
-- from: models/issues/issue_project.go:134
rule RecordProjectChange {
    when: projects/IssueProjectChanged(issue, actor, old_project, new_project)
    ensures: Comment.created(issue: issue, poster: actor, kind: project,
                             old_project: old_project, project: new_project,
                             content: "", content_version: 0, created_at: now, updated_at: now)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- from: models/issues/issue.go:92
invariant IndexUniquePerRepository {
    for a in Issues:
        for b in Issues:
            (a != b and a.repository = b.repository) implies a.index != b.index
}

invariant IndexIsPositive {
    for i in Issues:
        i.index >= 1
}

invariant ClosedIssuesHaveCloseTime {
    for i in Issues:
        i.status = closed implies i.closed_at != null
}

invariant LabelHasExactlyOneOwner {
    for l in Labels:
        (l.repository = null) != (l.organization = null)
}

-- Labels on an issue come from its repository or that repository's organization.
invariant IssueLabelsInScope {
    for i in Issues:
        i.labels.all(l => l.repository = i.repository or l.organization = i.repository.owner_org)
}

-- At most one label per exclusive scope on an issue.
invariant ExclusiveScopeHoldsOneLabel {
    for i in Issues:
        i.labels.all(a => i.labels.all(b => (a != b and a.is_exclusive and b.is_exclusive and a.scope != "") implies a.scope != b.scope))
}

invariant MilestoneInSameRepository {
    for i in Issues:
        i.milestone != null implies i.milestone.repository = i.repository
}

invariant PinLimit {
    for p in IssuePins:
        p.position >= 1 and p.position <= config.max_pinned
}

invariant OneStopwatchPerUser {
    for a in Stopwatches:
        for b in Stopwatches:
            (a != b) implies a.user != b.user
}

invariant NoSelfDependency {
    for d in IssueDependencies:
        d.issue != d.blocker
}

invariant NoMutualDependency {
    for a in IssueDependencies:
        for b in IssueDependencies:
            not (a.issue = b.blocker and a.blocker = b.issue)
}

invariant OneReactionPerUserEmojiTarget {
    for a in Reactions:
        for b in Reactions:
            (a != b and a.user = b.user and a.issue = b.issue and a.comment = b.comment) implies a.emoji != b.emoji
}

invariant ReactionsFromAllowedSet {
    for r in Reactions:
        r.emoji in config.allowed_reactions
}

invariant AttachmentsStayInRepository {
    for a in Attachments:
        a.issue != null implies a.issue.repository = a.repository
}

invariant CommentAttachmentsBelongToItsIssue {
    for a in Attachments:
        a.comment != null implies a.issue = a.comment.issue
}

invariant TrackedTimeIsPositive {
    for t in TrackedTimes:
        t.amount >= 0.seconds
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Actor Declarations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- Anyone who can read the repository's issues or pull requests. Anonymous
-- visitors of public repositories are included through `access` (see REQUEST).
actor TrackerReader {
    within: repositories/Repository
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_tracker(this, within)
}

-- Anyone who can read this issue (or PR conversation).
actor IssueReader {
    within: Issue
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_read_issue(this, within)
}

-- A user with write access to the issue's unit: closes, labels, assigns,
-- locks, sets milestones, due dates and dependencies.
actor IssueTriager {
    within: Issue
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_triage(this, within)
}

-- A repository admin (pins, deletes).
actor IssueAdmin {
    within: Issue
    identified_by: accounts/User where is_repo_admin(this, within.repository)
}

-- A user who can write issues or pull requests: manages labels and milestones.
actor TrackerManager {
    within: repositories/Repository
    identified_by: accounts/User where can_manage_tracker(this, within)
}

-- Shared actors: access/RepoAdmin, organizations/OrgOwner, access/SiteAdmin.

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The repository's issue / PR list and the "new issue" form.
surface IssueTracker {
    facing reader: TrackerReader
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    let issues = Issues where repository = repository
    let pins = IssuePins where repository = repository
    let repo_labels = Labels where repository = repository and archived_at = null
    let repo_milestones = Milestones where repository = repository
    let templates = IssueTemplates where repository = repository and is_valid

    exposes:
        for i in issues:
            i.index
            i.title
            i.status
            i.is_pull
            i.poster.name
            i.labels
            i.milestone.name
            i.assignees
            i.num_comments
            i.deadline
            i.is_overdue
            i.num_tasks
            i.num_tasks_done
            i.created_at
            i.updated_at
        for p in pins:
            p.issue.title
            p.position
        for l in repo_labels:
            l.name
            l.color
            l.description
            l.is_exclusive
        for m in repo_milestones:
            m.name
            m.status
            m.deadline
            m.num_open_issues
            m.num_closed_issues
            m.completeness
            m.is_overdue
        for t in templates:
            t.name
            t.about
            t.title
            t.labels
            t.fields
        IssueTemplateConfig.blank_issues_enabled
        IssueTemplateConfig.contact_links
        config.max_pinned

    provides:
        UserOpensIssue(reader, repository, title, content, labels, milestone, assignees, deadline, project, attachments, template)
            when not repository.is_archived
        UserUploadsAttachment(reader, repository, name, size, head_bytes)
            when config.attachments_enabled and not repository.is_archived

    @guarantee FilteringIsLocalToTheRepository
        -- The list filters by state (open / closed / all), labels (include and
        -- exclude, exclusive scopes collapse), milestone, project, assignee,
        -- poster, mentioned / created / assigned-to-me / review-requested, and
        -- keyword; archived labels' issues are hidden from the label filter
        -- unless asked for. Search across repositories is `discovery`.

    @guarantee TemplateChooser
        -- When the default branch has valid templates or contact links, "new
        -- issue" offers a chooser; when `blank_issues_enabled` is false a blank
        -- form is not offered (and posting one is refused, see UserOpensIssue). Invalid template files are reported to the
        -- reader instead of silently ignored. Templates are looked up in
        -- ISSUE_TEMPLATE / issue_template under the repository root,
        -- .forgejo/, .gitea/, .github/, .gitlab/ and docs/.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/issues, /pulls, /issues/new, /issues/new/choose,
        --   /issues/search, /issues/posters, /issues/suggestions, /labels, /milestones,
        --   /milestone/{id}, POST /issues/new, POST /issues/attachments,
        --   POST /issues/attachments/remove; badges /badges/issues*.svg.
        -- API: GET/POST /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues, GET /issues/pinned,
        --   /pulls/pinned, /new_pin_allowed, /issue_templates, /issue_config,
        --   /issue_config/validate, /labels, /labels/{id}, /milestones,
        --   /milestones/{id}, GET /issues/comments (repo-wide comment list).
}

-- One issue's page for anyone who can read it.
surface IssueConversation {
    facing reader: IssueReader
    context issue: Issue

    let visible_times = issue.tracked_times where is_deleted = false and user = reader

    exposes:
        issue.index
        issue.title
        issue.content
        issue.status
        issue.closed_at
        issue.is_locked
        issue.is_pull
        issue.ref
        issue.poster.name
        issue.labels
        issue.milestone.name
        issue.assignees
        issue.deadline
        issue.is_overdue
        issue.is_pinned
        issue.participants
        issue.created_at
        issue.updated_at
        issue.num_tasks
        issue.num_tasks_done
        for c in issue.comments:
            c.kind
            c.poster.name
            c.content
            c.created_at
            c.updated_at
            c.is_edited
            c.label.name
            c.label_added
            c.deleted_label_name
            c.label_is_deleted
            c.old_milestone.name
            c.new_milestone.name
            c.deleted_old_milestone_name
            c.deleted_new_milestone_name
            c.old_milestone_is_deleted
            c.new_milestone_is_deleted
            c.assignee.name
            c.assignee_removed
            c.old_title
            c.new_title
            c.old_ref
            c.new_ref
            c.dependent_issue.title
            c.commit_sha
            c.ref_issue.title
            c.ref_action
            role_in_repo(c.poster, issue)
            for r in c.reactions:
                r.emoji
                r.user.name
            for a in c.attachments:
                a.name
                a.size
        for r in issue.issue_reactions:
            r.emoji
            r.user.name
        for a in issue.attachments:
            a.name
            a.size
        for d in issue.blocked_by:
            d.blocker.title
            d.blocker.status
        for d in issue.blocking:
            d.issue.title
            d.issue.status
        for t in visible_times:
            t.amount
            t.created_at
        for h in issue.history:
            h.editor.name
            h.edited_at
            h.content
            h.is_deleted

    provides:
        UserViewsIssue(reader, issue)
        UserComments(reader, issue, content, attachments)
            when not issue.is_locked and not issue.repository.is_archived
        UserReactsToIssue(reader, issue, emoji)
            when not issue.repository.is_archived
        UserReactsToComment(reader, issue, comment, emoji)
            when not issue.repository.is_archived
        UserRemovesReaction(reader, issue, reaction)
        UserSetsIssueSubscription(reader, issue, subscriber, watching)
        UserChangesIssueTitle(reader, issue, title)
            when reader = issue.poster
        UserEditsIssueBody(reader, issue, content, seen_version)
            when reader = issue.poster
        UserChangesIssueRef(reader, issue, ref)
            when reader = issue.poster and not issue.is_pull and not issue.is_locked
        UserClosesIssue(reader, issue)
            when reader = issue.poster and issue.status = open and not issue.is_locked
        UserReopensIssue(reader, issue)
            when reader = issue.poster and issue.status = closed and not issue.is_locked
        UserEditsComment(reader, issue, comment, content, seen_version)
        UserDeletesComment(reader, issue, comment)
        UserHidesContentRevision(reader, issue, revision)
        UserStartsStopwatch(reader, issue)
            when may_track_time(reader, issue)
        UserStopsStopwatch(reader, issue, stopwatch)
        UserCancelsStopwatch(reader, issue, stopwatch)
        UserAddsTime(reader, issue, amount)
            when may_track_time(reader, issue)
        UserDeletesTime(reader, issue, time)
        UserResetsOwnTime(reader, issue)
        UserDeletesAttachment(reader, issue, attachment)
        UserRenamesAttachment(reader, issue, attachment, name)

    @guarantee ReferencesRespectVisibility
        -- Cross-reference entries whose origin the reader cannot read are not
        -- shown, and a blocker the reader cannot read is shown only as
        -- "an issue you cannot see".

    @guarantee OwnTimeOnly
        -- Readers who cannot triage see only their own tracked time in time
        -- listings; triagers and site admins see everyone's.

    @guarantee LockedConversationExplained
        -- On a locked issue a reader without write access is told the
        -- conversation is locked (with the reason) instead of a comment box.

    @guarantee OriginalAuthorShown
        -- Where the migrations addon recorded an original author for the
        -- issue, a comment or a reaction (a migrations/ExternalAuthorship
        -- pointing at it), the item renders "originally by <external_name> on
        -- <source>"; assignees the source named that are not local accounts
        -- (migrations/ExternalAssignee) are listed by name beside the
        -- assignees. The core keeps no import fields of its own.

    @guarantee RoleBadges
        -- Each poster is badged poster / owner / member / collaborator /
        -- contributor (has a merged PR) / first-time contributor.

    @guidance
        -- Web: GET /{owner}/{repo}/issues/{index} (also /pulls/{index}),
        --   /issues/{index}/content-history/{overview,list,detail},
        --   /issues/{index}/attachments, /attachments/{uuid}, /comments/{id}/attachments,
        --   POST /issues/{index}/{title,content,ref,comments,watch,reactions/{react|unreact},
        --   times/add,times/{id}/delete,times/stopwatch/{toggle,cancel},
        --   content-history/soft-delete}, POST /comments/{id}, /comments/{id}/delete,
        --   /comments/{id}/reactions/{action}.
        -- API: GET/PATCH /repos/{o}/{r}/issues/{index}, GET/POST /issues/{index}/comments,
        --   GET /issues/{index}/timeline, GET/PATCH/DELETE /issues/comments/{id},
        --   GET/POST/DELETE /issues/{index}/reactions, /issues/comments/{id}/reactions,
        --   /issues/{index}/assets[/{id}], /issues/comments/{id}/assets[/{id}],
        --   /issues/{index}/times[/{id}], /issues/{index}/stopwatch/{start,stop,delete},
        --   /issues/{index}/subscriptions[/check|/{user}], GET /issues/{index}/dependencies,
        --   GET /issues/{index}/blocks, GET /issues/{index}/labels.
}

-- What a triager can additionally do on an issue.
surface IssueTriage {
    facing triager: IssueTriager
    context issue: Issue

    exposes:
        issue.labels
        issue.milestone
        issue.assignees
        issue.deadline
        issue.is_locked
        for t in issue.active_times:
            t.user.name
            t.logged_by.name
            t.amount
        for w in issue.watches:
            w.user.name
            w.is_watching

    provides:
        UserClosesIssue(triager, issue) when issue.status = open
        UserReopensIssue(triager, issue) when issue.status = closed
        UserChangesIssueTitle(triager, issue, title)
        UserEditsIssueBody(triager, issue, content, seen_version)
        UserComments(triager, issue, content, attachments)
            when not issue.repository.is_archived
        TriagerAddsLabel(triager, issue, added)
        TriagerRemovesLabel(triager, issue, removed)
        TriagerReplacesLabels(triager, issue, labels)
        TriagerClearsLabels(triager, issue)
        TriagerSetsMilestone(triager, issue, target)
        TriagerTogglesAssignee(triager, issue, assignee)
        TriagerReplacesAssignees(triager, issue, wanted)
        TriagerSetsDueDate(triager, issue, deadline)
        TriagerRemovesDueDate(triager, issue)
        TriagerLocksIssue(triager, issue, reason) when not issue.is_locked
        TriagerUnlocksIssue(triager, issue) when issue.is_locked
        TriagerAddsDependency(triager, issue, blocker)
            when dependencies_enabled(issue.repository)
        TriagerRemovesDependency(triager, issue, dependency)
            when dependencies_enabled(issue.repository)

    @guarantee ClosingBlockedIssueExplained
        -- Closing an issue with open blockers is refused with a message naming
        -- the blocking issues; batch close stops at the first such issue.

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/issues/{labels,milestone,assignee,status} (batch,
        --   `issue_ids`), /issues/{index}/{deadline,lock,unlock,dependency/add,dependency/delete}.
        -- API: PATCH /issues/{index} (state, milestone, assignees, due_date, unset_due_date),
        --   POST /issues/{index}/deadline, POST/PUT/DELETE /issues/{index}/labels,
        --   DELETE /issues/{index}/labels/{id}, PUT/DELETE /issues/{index}/lock,
        --   POST/DELETE /issues/{index}/dependencies, POST/DELETE /issues/{index}/blocks.
}

-- Repository admins: pinning, deleting, and logging time for others.
surface IssueAdministration {
    facing admin: IssueAdmin
    context issue: Issue

    exposes:
        issue.is_pinned
        config.max_pinned

    provides:
        RepoAdminPinsIssue(admin, issue) when not issue.is_pinned
        RepoAdminUnpinsIssue(admin, issue) when issue.is_pinned
        RepoAdminDeletesIssue(admin, issue)
        AdminAddsTimeForUser(admin, issue, user, amount, at)
            when may_track_time(admin, issue)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /issues/{index}/pin, DELETE /issues/unpin/{index}, POST /issues/move_pin,
        --   POST /issues/{index}/delete, POST /issues/delete (batch); the web
        --   "add time" form gains a user and date picker for repository admins.
        -- API: POST/DELETE /issues/{index}/pin, PATCH /issues/{index}/pin/{position},
        --   DELETE /issues/{index}, POST /issues/{index}/times (user_name, created).
}

surface PinOrdering {
    facing admin: access/RepoAdmin
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    let pins = IssuePins where repository = repository

    exposes:
        for p in pins:
            p.issue.title
            p.position
            p.is_pull

    provides:
        RepoAdminMovesPin(admin, repository, pin, position)
}

-- Labels and milestones of a repository.
surface TrackerSettings {
    facing manager: TrackerManager
    context repository: repositories/Repository

    let all_labels = Labels where repository = repository
    let org_labels = Labels where organization = repository.owner_org
    let all_milestones = Milestones where repository = repository

    exposes:
        for l in all_labels:
            l.name
            l.description
            l.color
            l.is_exclusive
            l.is_archived
        for l in org_labels:
            l.name
            l.color
        for m in all_milestones:
            m.name
            m.description
            m.status
            m.deadline
            m.completeness
        for t in LabelTemplates:
            t.name
            t.description

    provides:
        TrackerManagerCreatesLabel(manager, repository, name, description, color, is_exclusive)
            when not repository.is_archived
        TrackerManagerEditsLabel(manager, repository, label, name, description, color, is_exclusive, is_archived)
        TrackerManagerDeletesLabel(manager, repository, label)
        TrackerManagerInitialisesLabels(manager, repository, template)
            when not repository.is_archived
        TrackerManagerCreatesMilestone(manager, repository, name, description, deadline)
            when not repository.is_archived
        TrackerManagerEditsMilestone(manager, repository, milestone, name, description, deadline)
        TrackerManagerClosesMilestone(manager, repository, milestone)
        TrackerManagerReopensMilestone(manager, repository, milestone)
        TrackerManagerDeletesMilestone(manager, repository, milestone)

    @guidance
        -- Web: POST /{owner}/{repo}/labels/{new,edit,delete,initialize},
        --   /milestones/new, /milestones/{id}/edit, /milestones/{id}/{open|close},
        --   /milestones/delete.
        -- API: POST /repos/{o}/{r}/labels, PATCH/DELETE /labels/{id},
        --   POST /milestones, PATCH/DELETE /milestones/{id} (state in PATCH).
}

surface OrganizationLabels {
    facing owner: organizations/OrgOwner
    context organization: organizations/Organization

    let labels = Labels where organization = organization

    exposes:
        for l in labels:
            l.name
            l.description
            l.color
            l.is_exclusive
            l.is_archived

    provides:
        OrgOwnerCreatesLabel(owner, organization, name, description, color, is_exclusive)
        OrgOwnerEditsLabel(owner, organization, label, name, description, color, is_exclusive, is_archived)
        OrgOwnerDeletesLabel(owner, organization, label)
        OrgOwnerInitialisesLabels(owner, organization, template)

    @guidance
        -- Web: /org/{org}/settings/labels{,/new,/edit,/delete,/initialize}.
        -- API: GET /orgs/{org}/labels (members), POST, GET/PATCH/DELETE /orgs/{org}/labels/{id}.
}

-- A signed-in user's own time tracking across repositories.
surface MyTimeTracking {
    facing user: accounts/User

    let running = Stopwatches where user = user
    let mine = TrackedTimes where user = user and is_deleted = false

    exposes:
        for sw in running:
            sw.issue.title
            sw.elapsed
        for t in mine:
            t.issue.title
            t.amount
            t.created_at

    provides:
        UserStopsStopwatch(user, stopwatch.issue, stopwatch)
        UserCancelsStopwatch(user, stopwatch.issue, stopwatch)

    @guidance
        -- Web: navbar stopwatch, /user/stopwatches.
        -- API: GET /user/stopwatches, GET /user/times.
}

surface SiteTimeAdministration {
    facing admin: access/SiteAdmin

    exposes:
        for t in TrackedTimes:
            t.user.name
            t.issue.title
            t.amount

    provides:
        UserDeletesTime(admin, time.issue, time)
        AdminAddsTimeForUser(admin, issue, user, amount, at)
        UserSetsIssueSubscription(admin, issue, subscriber, watching)
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Deferred Specifications
------------------------------------------------------------

deferred resolve_mentions                 -- see: modules/references/references.go mention grammar
deferred cross_references                 -- see: models/issues/issue_xref.go verifyReferencedIssue
deferred commit_references                -- see: modules/references/references.go keyword grammar
deferred template_is_valid                -- see: modules/issue/template/template.go Validate
deferred is_allowed_file                  -- see: modules/upload (extensions, MIME types, wildcards)

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Requests to other modules
------------------------------------------------------------
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.owner_org: used to scope organization labels (fixed name, listed for completeness)
-- REQUEST repositories/RepoUnit (issues) config: enable_timetracker, allow_only_contributors_to_track_time, enable_dependencies — read here as timetracker_enabled / only_contributors_track_time / dependencies_enabled; defaults come from this module's default_* config
-- REQUEST repositories/Repository.close_issues_via_commit_in_any_branch: keyword closing on non-default branches (default DEFAULT_CLOSE_ISSUES_VIA_COMMITS_IN_ANY_BRANCH = false)
-- REQUEST repositories/RepositoryDeleted(repository): trigger this module reacts to
-- REQUEST repositories/Watch.watches_issues: per-repository custom watch selection (issues / PRs) used for implicit issue subscription
-- REQUEST code/PushReceived(push) with push.repository, push.pusher, push.branch and push.commits (sha, message, timestamp)
-- REQUEST pulls/PullRequestMerged(pull_request, merger) with pull_request.issue
-- REQUEST pulls/MergeClosesReferencedIssues guidance: Forgejo does NOT ignore open dependencies when a merge closes a referenced issue — the close fails and the error is swallowed (services/pull/merge.go:303), so the issue stays open; issues/ApplyResolvedReference models that
-- REQUEST pulls: issues_closed_by(pr) / issues_reopened_by(pr) should be the latest closes/reopens Comment (ref_issue = pr.issue, ref_action) per target issue, from issues' cross-reference entries
-- REQUEST pulls: PR conversations are created as issues/Issue (is_pull = true) and must set index: next_issue_index(repository), content_version: 0, labels/assignees/mentioned_users/read_by, created_at/updated_at; pulls' Comment.created calls should also set content_version / created_at / updated_at
-- REQUEST webhooks / actions: subscribe to this module's trigger names and arities as listed in the header (e.g. IssueCommentCreated(issue, comment, doer, mentions), IssueAssigneeChanged(issue, doer, assignee, removed, comment), IssueClosed(issue, doer, comment)); there is no IssueAssigneeAdded / CommentCreated / IssueEdited trigger
-- REQUEST access: an anonymous-visitor actor usable in TrackerReader / IssueReader surfaces for public repositories
-- REQUEST accounts/UserBlock: is_blocked(blocker, user), including organizations blocking users
-- REQUEST releases/Release: links Attachments via Attachment.release; release attachment type list is releases' config
-- REQUEST moderation: reacts to IssueContentChanged / IssueCommentEdited / IssueCommentDeleted / IssueDeleted to keep shadow copies of reported content
-- REQUEST quota: attachment uploads are subject to the `size:assets:attachments:issues` quota subject
-- REQUEST releases: web release uploads that are never saved into a release (UserLinksUploadToRelease) now expire via issues/OrphanUploadExpires after issues' config.orphan_attachment_expiry; worth a note in that rule's guidance
-- REQUEST pulls: on a locked PR conversation the poster may still change title and description but not close / reopen or retarget; pulls/UserClosesPullRequest and UserReopensPullRequest should require `not issue.is_locked or can_triage(user, issue)` (issues decision 1)
-- REQUEST pulls: reactions on a locked PR conversation are open to every reader (issues decision 2); issues/UserReactsToIssue / UserReactsToComment no longer check the lock
